From: Swift Linux <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Drop the devel run target when cross compiling

gjs_console comes from pkg-config:

    gjs_console = gjs_dep.get_variable(pkgconfig: 'gjs_console')

which answers with a path on the target - /usr/bin/gjs-console. That is
the right answer for conf.set('GJS', gjs_console), whose value becomes
the launcher's interpreter line and is only ever resolved on the device.

run_target is the other consumer, and it needs the same path to name a
program on the build machine. Cross compiling, it does not:

    src/meson.build:55:0: ERROR: Program '/usr/bin/gjs-console' not
    found or not executable

'devel' runs the freshly built application out of the build tree, so a
cross build has no use for it even if the lookup were satisfied - the
binary it would launch is for another architecture. Guarding it leaves
the launcher configuration untouched.

--- a/src/meson.build
+++ b/src/meson.build
@@ -52,8 +52,10 @@
   install_dir: decibels_bindir
 )

-run_target(
-  'devel',
-  command: [gjs_console, '-m', app_launcher],
-  depends: [src_res, data_res]
-)
+if not meson.is_cross_build()
+  run_target(
+    'devel',
+    command: [gjs_console, '-m', app_launcher],
+    depends: [src_res, data_res]
+  )
+endif
